# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Minicube64 -- Analogue Pocket core
#
# Derived from C:/Code/Wasm4/VexiiRiscv/ap_core.qsf, a Pocket core that builds
# and runs on hardware.  Taken from it: the device, the pin/location
# assignments, the bridge/framework settings.  Replaced: the source file list,
# which was Wasm4's (VexiiRiscv, the PSRAM cart interface, a second CPU PLL,
# the seed sweeps).
#
# The file list is at the END of this file, under "Source file list", so it is
# the one place to edit when a source is added.
#
# The project lives in rtl/ (ap_core.qpf/.qsf sit next to the sources), so every
# path in this file is relative to rtl/ -- that is why they read "mc64_top.sv"
# and not "rtl/mc64_top.sv". Compile from rtl/:  quartus_sh --flow compile ap_core
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

